# The lope tree PAX carries as /bin/lope (px54; tools/mklope builds it).
#
# lope is the directory jumper in wolf: the maintainer's gump ported and
# renamed (ruling #91, Track 13), a store of visited directories with a
# decaying score, a fuzzy matcher, `g`/`gi`, and shell hooks that record
# every `cd` and jump on a word that names no command. Ruling #91 R4:
# lope is preinstalled on PAX beside pelt and boreutils, and the console
# shell runs `lope init pelt` (/etc/pax-run's `/bin/env ENV=/etc/shrc
# /bin/sh -i -m`, /etc/shrc's `eval "$(lope init pelt)"`), so the
# no-prefix jump works at PAX's console through pelt's
# command_not_found_handle (sh21, pelt 90d7c64).
#
# lope trunk at the time of px54 (2026-10-20): 5ac37df (lp00's merge;
# its src/ is ee97741's), pinned in its own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf
# 0.2.33 / lupin 0.1.54 / wolf-std cceda63. tools/mklope builds it with
# THAT toolchain (the archive by the digest lope names, the std tree at
# the commit it names), not with kernel/wolf.pin's, as tools/mkpelt
# builds pelt. lope is PRIVATE: tools/mklope fetches it from
# PAX_LOPE_REPO when set (CI's checkout with the org's token; a clone
# from a bundle on kasumi).
#
# The static binary depends on the libc.a it links (lp00): built in
# kasumi's localhost/px13-ubuntu (image ad8964505189: Ubuntu 24.04.5,
# libc6-dev 2.39-0ubuntu8.9, gcc 13.3.0), lp00's tools/mkstatic gave
# f9a2f064077f6bb33ede9219608b6fe72d4a45a66c84f61f3f9d9e5e94f5066c,
# 14,426,728 bytes, twice.
LOPE_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/lope
LOPE_REV=5ac37df22866e8fd418c67b611f48ff30e8a2630
